[section=building][section_title1]Building[/section_title1]
See [url=https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/contributing/development/compiling/introduction_to_the_buildsystem.html]Introduction to the buildsystem[/url] for the required tools to building this GDExtension in your machine.

You can also build using the Dockerfile in the repository.

After getting the required tools, you can build the GDExtension with:

[codeblocks]
[bash]
scons platform=<platform>
[/bash]
[/codeblocks]
Replace [code]<platform>[/code] with the target platform:
[ul]
[*][code]linux[/code] for Linux systems;
[*][code]windows[/code] for Windows systems;
[*][code]android[/code] for Android systems.
[/ul]
After finishing the build, you will be able to find the binaries in [code]bin/[/code] folder, copy then to the [code]addons/rmlui/bin/[/code] folder in your project, overwritting existing binaries if already exists.
[/section]
[section=build-options][section_title2]Build Options[/section_title2]
With the SCons build system, you can pass additional flags when building the extension:

[h3][code]svg_plugin=<yes|no>[/code][/h3]
Defaults to [code]yes[/code]

By default, the extension builds with SVG support, using [url=https://github.com/sammycage/lunasvg]lunasvg[/url], but you can pass [code]svg_plugin=no[/code] to disable SVG support.

[h3][code]element_reference_strict=<yes|no>[/code][/h3]
Defaults to [code]no[/code]

[class RMLElement] is a reference to a element inside the RmlUi document's tree, all the API always returns a non-null instance of it, but in case of querying elements which doesn't exist in the tree, for example, RMLElement references a null element.

By default, when trying to handle RMLElement instances with null reference, it does nothing and/or returns default values.

But you can enable strict element referencing by passing [code]element_reference_strict=yes[/code] flag to the scons, meaning that any atempt of handling RMLElement instances with null reference, will print an error and pause the execution on debug builds.

In both cases, you can check if the instance is valid with [method RMLElement.is_valid].
[/section]